    "Eye is a round disc; the real eye is a horizontally oval slit with a raised supraorbital ridge.",
    "Gill slits 1-4, spiracles, mouth, labial furrows and nostrils are painted cues; only the fifth gill slit has relief.",
    "Caudal subterminal notch is not modelled; the caudal is a low rounded heterocercal blade.",
    "Paired fins are single thin shells so the spotted dorsal pattern also appears on their ventral face.",
